Acquisition rationale must identify achievable benefits exceeding premium and integration costs.|Buying technology shortens development time but raises execution risk.|Strategic fit alone proves positive NPV?|No|Yes|Only for cash deals
Horizontal deals combine competitors; vertical deals combine supply-chain stages; conglomerate deals span different businesses.|A manufacturer buys its component supplier.|This is primarily…?|Vertical integration|Horizontal integration|A share split
Buy-side processes evaluate and negotiate; sell-side processes prepare, market, and compare offers.|An auction attracts bids but requires diligence and comparable terms.|Highest headline bid always gives best seller outcome?|No|Yes|Only in auctions
Target screening prioritises strategic fit, economics, scale, risks, and feasibility.|A target has strong products but incompatible systems and heavy debt.|Screening should consider…?|Integration and funding feasibility|Only sales growth|Only brand recognition
Due diligence tests commercial, financial, tax, and legal claims with evidence.|Reported recurring profit contains large one-time gains.|Financial diligence should…?|Reconcile sustainable earnings and cash|Accept the headline|Ignore footnotes
Deal valuation distinguishes stand-alone value, synergies, premium, and claims.|Target value ₹100 plus buyer benefits ₹30 sets a ceiling before integration costs.|Paying ₹140 automatically creates buyer value?|No|Yes|Only if financed cheaply
Synergies add combined benefits; dis-synergies and integration costs subtract them.|Benefit PV ₹20 less integration ₹8 and lost-customer PV ₹5 leaves ₹7.|Net benefit is…?|₹7|₹20|₹33
Cash, shares, and mixed consideration allocate financing and future-performance exposure differently.|Stock payment gives target owners exposure to the combined company.|Stock payment is economically costless?|No|Yes|Only when no cash leaves
Acquisition financing combines funding sources and their debt-service, dilution, and flexibility consequences.|New borrowing funds a purchase but increases required payments.|Funding availability proves deal attractiveness?|No|Yes|Only if interest is low
Accretion raises pro-forma EPS; dilution lowers it; neither alone measures economic value.|A cheap debt-funded purchase raises EPS while overpaying for cash flows.|Accretion guarantees positive NPV?|No|Yes|Only after closing
Merger models integrate statements, funding, purchase accounting, shares, and synergies.|Extra amortisation reduces combined profit after acquisition.|Ignore purchase accounting in EPS forecasts?|No|Yes|Only for cash deals
Price adjustments reconcile agreed debt, cash, and working-capital conditions at completion.|Delivered working capital is ₹5 below an agreed target.|Subject to terms, price may…?|Be adjusted for the shortfall|Remain higher automatically|Ignore operating balances
Earn-outs tie future payments to specified performance; terms can create disputes and incentives.|Seller receives additional cash if revenue exceeds a threshold.|An earn-out eliminates all valuation disagreement?|No|Yes|Only for startups
LBOs use substantial debt; management buyouts include management ownership and possible conflicts.|Debt service limits investment flexibility in a buyout.|Leverage guarantees high equity returns?|No|Yes|Only when bought cheaply
Divestitures sell assets; carve-outs separate businesses; spin-offs distribute ownership; split-offs exchange specified claims.|A parent distributes subsidiary shares to owners.|A spin-off necessarily raises cash for the parent?|No|Yes|Only if listed
Takeover defences alter acquisition feasibility; activism seeks changes through shareholder influence.|A defence protects management but may block an attractive offer.|Evaluate…?|Owner interests and governance context|Only management preference|Only bidder size
Restructuring changes claims or terms to restore viability and allocate losses.|Lenders extend maturity and exchange debt for equity.|This necessarily restores business profitability?|No|Yes|Only after legal approval
Insolvency waterfalls allocate recoveries by applicable law, security, priority, and proceedings.|Asset recoveries cover secured creditors but leave limited residual value.|Equity normally has a prior claim over all debt?|No|Yes|Only if founders object
Integration tracking compares realised benefits and costs with deal assumptions.|Promised savings ₹20 yield only ₹8 after execution delays.|Review should focus on…?|Net realised value and corrective action|Only announcement-day EPS|Only deal size
